From: Oichkatzelesfrettschen <151315375+Oichkatzelesfrettschen@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: reload on attrib events

watchdog 7 reports a metadata-only change (touch, utime, chmod) as a
FileAttribEvent; earlier releases reported FileModifiedEvent. The monitor
handled only created, modified, moved and deleted events, so touching a
watched file no longer triggered a reload:

  tests/test_it.py::test_myapp_reloads_when_touching_ini
  RuntimeError: timeout waiting for change to file=...

An attrib event on a watched path now takes the same route as a modified event.

--- a/src/hupper/watchdog.py
+++ b/src/hupper/watchdog.py
@@ -61,3 +61,8 @@
 
     def on_deleted(self, event):
         self._check(event.src_path)
+
+    def on_attrib(self, event):
+        # watchdog >= 7 reports a metadata-only change (touch, utime, chmod)
+        # as an attrib event instead of a modified event.
+        self._check(event.src_path)
